Found in read-only bug hunt (langertha-reviewer, 2026-09-25). Confirmed by code reading.

lib/Langertha/Plugin/Langfuse.pm plugin_after_llm_response (~line 460): create_generation(trace_id, name => "generation-$iteration", start_time, end_time) only. $data is the Langertha::Response and has model, usage (Langertha::Usage), content, tool_calls, timing; none of it reaches the generation. create_generation has no completionStartTime either. The engine-level Role::Langfuse around simple_chat does send model + usage + completionStartTime, so the two integrations disagree.

Also: _iter_start / _trace_id are single slots on the plugin, so concurrent simple_chat_f calls on one Chat overwrite each other start time (minor).

Fix: pass model => $data->model (when has_model), usage => {input, output, total} from $data->usage, output => content (or to_hash), input => the conversation captured in plugin_before_llm_call, completion_start_time from ttft_seconds, mirroring Role::Langfuse. Test with a mocked Chat run and assert the batch payload.
